\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Library Manager Josh Murray invited the community to attend \ldblquote The Magic Life of Houdini\rdblquote  featuring Duffy Hudson on Tuesday, July 22, 2025, from 6:00 PM to 7:00 PM. He thanked the City of Manhattan Beach for being a great partner and announced that this would be his final City Council meeting, with the new Library Manager to be introduced at the next meeting.\line\line Downtown Manhattan Beach Business and Professional Association representative Maureen McBride announced a "Throwback to 1985\rdblquote  celebration in honor of the Association\rquote s 40th anniversary, taking place on July 22, 2025.\line\line Cultural Arts Coordinator Andrew Booras invited the community to two free Shakespeare by the Sea performances \ldblquote As You Like It\rdblquote  on July 17, 2025, and \ldblquote Julius Caesar\rdblquote  on July 18, 2025, both at 7:00 PM in Polliwog Park. He also invited the public to attend the Annual Community Exhibition opening reception at the Manhattan Beach Art Center on July 25, 2025, from 5:00 PM to 7:00 PM.\line\line Shakespeare by the Sea Board Member Dency Nelson announced that Manhattan Beach was one of the original five cities to host performances when the program began 25 years ago, and thanked the City Council, staff, and residents for their continued support over the years.\line\line\pard Sports Supervisor Archie Sherman announced the 57th Annual Manhattan Beach Open Tennis Tournament, taking place from July 17-20, 2025, at Live Oak Park, Mira Costa High School, with finals held at the Manhattan Country Club. He also announced that the 62nd Annual International Surf Festival will kick off on August 1, 2025.\cf1\i0\f1\par
